From 61af3a49e1519947f112891e2fec08d26c07e481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: horizon-prism <horizon-prism@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:44:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Horizon instance type skeleton (M1)

Register InstanceType=Horizon and load it as HorizonInstance, a
MinecraftInstance subclass that keeps the Prism game dir, saves, screenshots
and Microsoft account, but drops the Java assumptions:

- horizon.json is the source of truth for the Horizon side (channel,
  client/preparer versions, launch_api/output_version/native_hooks pins);
- MinecraftInstance::loadSpecificSettings() rewrites InstanceType to
  OneSix, so HorizonInstance restores Horizon after the base call;
- no update task, no PackProfile traits, Horizon folders for resources,
  home and preparer root;
- launching ends in HorizonNotPrepared with a clear message instead of
  running the Java launch steps (real launching is M3, preparation M4).

Not compiled yet: this machine has no Qt 6, CMake or Ninja.
See fork/M1.md for the manual test procedure.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
